You tune a robot pick-and-place controller by changing numeric parameters only. Propose EXACTLY 4 different candidate patches in one reply: {"candidates": [ {"changes": {...}, "rationale": "...", "expected_effect": "..."}, ... ]}. Each 'changes' maps parameter names to new values within the stated min/max, using only these parameters: grip_force, grasp_hold_steps, retry_count, lift_speed, lift_height. Integer parameters (grasp_hold_steps, retry_count) are rounded to integers. The candidates must be DIVERSE: (a) at least one candidate changes exactly one parameter; (b) at least one candidate changes three or more parameters; (c) at least one candidate makes a larger step on some parameter and at least one makes only smaller steps. Every candidate will be tested by code on the analysis scenarios and the best one under a fixed rule is kept, so use the candidates to explore different ideas, not small variations of one idea. A good patch fixes the failing regions in the hypotheses WITHOUT breaking scenarios that already pass. Use the table of earlier candidates, if given: it shows what each tested candidate achieved overall and per hypothesis (fixed/total), so you can see which hypotheses still fail. You do not decide pass or fail.

Reply with a single JSON object matching this JSON Schema, and nothing else:
{"$defs": {"FixerOutput": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"changes": {"additionalProperties": {"type": "number"}, "title": "Changes", "type": "object"}, "rationale": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Rationale", "type": "string"}, "expected_effect": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Expected Effect", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["changes", "rationale", "expected_effect"], "title": "FixerOutput", "type": "object"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"candidates": {"items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/FixerOutput"}, "maxItems": 8, "minItems": 1, "title": "Candidates", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["candidates"], "title": "FixerCandidates", "type": "object"}

